. /**************************************************************************
> * H1: Gender Role Attitudes – Final Version                              *
> * Authors: [REDACTED], Saverio Lenzi                                    *
> **************************************************************************
> * CHANGE LOG (July 2025):
> * Following feedback, we revised the H1 analysis to produce 
> * a single testable result for H1. We retained only `id_gnorm_eq` as our 
> * outcome, which captures agreement with the statement:
> * "Best if man and woman work the same amount so they can share the responsib
> ility".
> * 
> * This variable offers the most direct and generalizable measure of 
> * support for gender equality in household roles. It avoids parenting-specifi
> c 
> * framings and best reflects the conceptual aim of H1.
> **************************************************************************/
. * clear all
. version 18

. set maxvar 10000


. 
. 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * INSTALL PACKAGES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. ssc install mdesc
checking mdesc consistency and verifying not already installed...
all files already exist and are up to date.

. 
. *-----------------------------
. * CONFIGURE FILE PATHS
. /*
> *-----------------------------
> if strpos("`c(pwd)'", "code") {
> global ROOT "`c(pwd)'/.."
> }
> else {
> global ROOT "`c(pwd)'"
> }
> global IN "$ROOT/data/raw" // folder, in which the original datasets are stor
> ed
> global DATA "$ROOT/data/derived" // folder for datasets
> global OUT "$ROOT/out" // folder for output (results, tables)
> 
> */
. 
. *============================================================================
> ===
. **# Data Preparation * 
